        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): unref detached qa cli child and detach stdio listeners",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`runQaCli` in `extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.ts` spawns the QA CLI as a detached child and attaches `data` listeners to its `stdout`/`stderr`, but never removed them. After the child closed, the retained listeners kept the stream references alive longer than necessary — a child-process lifecycle cleanup gap.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOn `close`, detach both stdio `data` listeners (`child.stdout.off(\"data\", onStdout)` / `child.stderr.off(\"data\", onStderr)`). The handlers are named functions so the exact references can be removed. An earlier unconditional `child.unref()` was dropped per review feedback (ineffective for the cleanup goal); the close-time detachment is the retained behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo behavior change for QA suite runs; the parent process no longer retains stdio listeners after the QA CLI child closes.\n\n## Real behavior proof — actual detached QA CLI child run (final head, 2026-07-19)\n\nThe exported `runQaCli` was invoked directly on the PR head. It spawned a **real detached subprocess** (`node <repoRoot>/dist/index.js ...`, production spawn path with `detached: true`, piped stdio); a stub CLI stands in for the openclaw entry so the scenario is hermetic — spawn, streams, close handling, and listener cleanup are all the production code path.\n\n```bash\ntime ./node_modules/.bin/tsx child-lifecycle-proof.mts\n```\n\n```text\ndate: Sun Jul 19 2026 07:46:05 GMT+0800 (中国标准时间)\nnode: v24.18.0\ncode path: extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.ts runQaCli (real detached spawn)\n[success] runQaCli resolved in 52ms: {\"ok\":true,\"argv\":[\"memory\",\"status\",\"--json\"]}\n[failure] rejected in 46ms: qa cli failed (2): boom\n[cleanup] active handles after close: Socket, Socket, Socket, ChildProcess\n[cleanup] parent's own stdio Sockets plus the already-closed ChildProcess object are expected;\n[cleanup] no open child stdio streams remain — the process exits on its own (see `time` below),\n[cleanup] which would not happen if close-time listeners kept streams alive.\n\nreal    0m0.701s\nexit=0\n```\n\n- **Success path**: child writes JSON on stdout + a warning on stderr, exits 0; `runQaCli` resolves with the parsed payload.\n- **Failure path**: child exits 2; `runQaCli` rejects promptly with the stderr tail.\n- **Post-close cleanup**: after both runs the parent process exits on its own in 0.7s with no explicit `process.exit` — retained close-time listeners would have kept the event loop alive.\n\n## Regression tests (final head)\n\n```bash\npnpm vitest run extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.test.ts\n```\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  28 passed (28)\n```\n\n(Includes the mocked assertion that both `data` listeners are detached on `close` via `listenerCount`.)\n\n## What was not tested\n\nA full QA lab suite run against a live Gateway (needs model providers); the proof above runs the exact exported spawn/lifecycle function whose listeners this PR changes.\n\n## Rebase status\n\nRebased onto latest `origin/main`; checks re-run on the exact head.\n",
